Then we define
\begin{equation}\label{hatShplus}
\hat{\Sigma}_{2,h}^\ast:=\{\tau\in H(\d, \Omega; \mathbb{S}), \tau|_K\in \hat{P}_2^\ast(K; \mathbb{S}) \text{ for  any }K\in\mathcal{T}_h\}.
\end{equation}
\begin{remark} For $n=2, 3$, we  recover the simplified   lowest order elements in \cite{Arnold-Winther-conforming} and  \cite{Arnold-Awanou-Winther}, respectively.
\end{remark}

\begin{proof} The dimension of the space $\Sigma_{K, k+n-1, b}$ reads
